# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NOTE: js/firebase-config.js IS tracked on purpose. A Firebase *web* API key is a
# public client identifier, not a secret — the site cannot load without it. Access is
# controlled by Firestore security rules, not by hiding this key.
# Do NOT add .htaccess here — it is required in the repo so GitHub Actions deploys it
# (it is Layer 1 of cache busting; see CLAUDE.md).

# Firebase Admin service account key — this one IS a real secret. NEVER commit it.
service-account.json
archive-scripts/service-account.json

# ─── ENTRANT PII — NEVER COMMIT ANY OF THIS ─────────────────────────────────
# This repo is PUBLIC, and deploy.yml uploads ./* to the public webroot. Anything
# committed here is published twice over: readable in git history forever, and
# downloadable from basic-bros-pga-pickems.com.
#
# These files hold real entrant email addresses and phone numbers (~137 unique
# emails and ~131 phone numbers as of 2026-07-31). Committing them would be a far
# worse leak than the Firestore exposure described under "Priority: PII Data Split"
# in CLAUDE.md, because it needs no API call at all — just a URL.
#
# The non-PII archives (standings_*.csv, scoreboard.csv, the ESPN/scores raw JSON)
# ARE tracked: they contain only names and golfer picks, which the public
# leaderboard already displays.
data-archive/**/picks.csv
data-archive/*picks_raw*.json
Picks/
